  "description": "A result cache for SQL Server and Azure SQL that sits in front of the database as a gateway. Clients connect to DaffyZoom as if it were SQL Server. Everything is relayed byte for byte, except repeats of slow queries on tables that rarely change, which are answered from an encrypted local cache in a fraction of the time. Fails closed: whenever it is unsure, the query goes to SQL Server.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "DaffyZoom",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-11T01:09:47.287Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "sKyDs+HydSmD+suNCxCh8J16LEy7bpDJ1EfMAXlXFM7S9n/5/72iVBSZpWwQf1ZEduOLv3a2WDtfk/ixW2smSw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 2471330,
  "projectUrl": "https://trobee.one/",
  "published": "2026-11-11T00:59:38.943Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0: first release. A result cache in front of SQL Server and Azure SQL, as a gateway: slow queries that repeat exactly are answered from an encrypted local copy, everything else is relayed byte for byte, and whenever DaffyZoom is unsure the query goes to SQL Server. Nothing is cached until a database has a policy: ttl mode (max age, a flush from the ETL job, a watermark poll, scheduled flushes, blackout windows, writes seen through DaffyZoom) or tracked mode (Change Tracking checked on every hit, as the client's own login). Prepared statements (sp_prepexec) are served with a handle SQL Server issued for the client's own session. Administration in T-SQL (EXEC daffyzoom.help), including daffyzoom.tracking, which shows Change Tracking as the caller's login sees it and the GRANT that fixes what is missing. The cache keeps within --cache-max-gb and what its disk can spare. Checked end to end against SQL Server 2022 with twelve drivers.",
